# Import Paths — MANDATORY

You MUST follow these rules. Do NOT use @/ for imports when the target lives inside the same top-level folder as the importing file.

## CRITICAL: Inside components/ — Use Relative Paths ONLY

**When the importing file is under `components/`** (web: `apps/web-app/components/`, mobile: `apps/mobile-app/components/`):

- **NEVER** use `@/components` to import another component from `components/`
- **ALWAYS** use relative paths (`./`, `../`, `../../`)

This applies to:
- `components/auth/` importing from `components/auth/`, `components/ui/`, etc.
- `components/pages/` importing from `components/auth/`, `components/ui/`, etc.
- `components/ui/` importing from `components/ui/`
- `components/shared/` importing from `components/`
- `components/navigation/` importing from `components/`
- Test files (`.test.tsx`) importing the component under test — use relative

### Examples

```tsx
// components/auth/AcceptInviteForm/AcceptInviteForm.tsx
// ✅ CORRECT
import AuthFormDivider from "../AuthFormDivider/AuthFormDivider";
import GoogleSignInButton from "../GoogleSignInButton/GoogleSignInButton";

// ❌ WRONG — NEVER do this inside components/
import { AuthFormDivider, GoogleSignInButton } from "@/components";
```

```tsx
// components/auth/InviteNotice/InviteNotice.tsx
// ✅ CORRECT
import Text from "../../ui/Text/Text";

// ❌ WRONG
import { Text } from "@/components";
```

```tsx
// components/pages/auth/InviteAcceptScreen/InviteAcceptScreen.tsx
// ✅ CORRECT — same top-level folder (components/)
import AcceptInviteForm from "../../auth/AcceptInviteForm/AcceptInviteForm";
import AcceptInviteInfo from "../../auth/AcceptInviteInfo/AcceptInviteInfo";
import AuthCardLayout from "../../auth/AuthCardLayout/AuthCardLayout";
import CrownLussoLogo from "../../auth/CrownLussoLogo/CrownLussoLogo";
import Text from "../../ui/Text/Text";

// ❌ WRONG
import { AcceptInviteForm, AcceptInviteInfo, AuthCardLayout, CrownLussoLogo, Text } from "@/components";
```

## When @/ IS Allowed

Use `@/` only when the import crosses top-level folders:
- `app/` importing from `components/`, `types/`, `constants/`, `services/`, `hooks/`, `utils/`
- `components/` importing from `types/`, `constants/`, `services/`, `hooks/`, `utils/`
- Test files importing `@/test-utils` (test-utils is outside components)

## Source of Truth

See `docs/import-patterns-guide.md` for the full guide. This rule enforces the "Component Internal Imports" section strictly.
